@startuml stack-decision
!theme plain
title Stack decision - Decision tree

skinparam backgroundColor #1a1a2e
skinparam defaultFontColor #eaeaea
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #0f3460
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4ecdc4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #16213e
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #e94560
skinparam ArrowColor #4ecdc4
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #16213e
skinparam NoteBorderColor #4ecdc4

start

:Project constraints;
note right
  - Free (0 EUR)
  - Nothing to install on work PC
  - Accessible anywhere (browser)
  - Rich editor (copy/paste images)
  - Career-proof (personal data)
  - Minimal phone battery impact
end note

if (Hosting?) then (paid cloud)
  :Cloud hosting rejected;
  stop
else (free)
  if (24/7 server availability?) then (personal PC)
    :PC must stay on\n(not practical);
    stop
  else (phone)
    :Phone is always on;
  endif
endif

:Android runtime choice;
note right
  Termux is the only mature
  free runtime on Android
  (full Linux without root).
end note

if (Backend language?) then
  :Phone-focused evaluation;
  note right
    | Language | RAM | Speed | Termux | Familiar? |
    | Go | ~10 MB | high | yes | yes |
    | Node.js | ~50 MB | good | yes | yes |
    | Python | ~80 MB | medium | yes | medium |
    | Bun | ~30 MB | high | partial | low |
  end note
  :Go selected;
  note right
    - Very light runtime footprint
    - Single static binary output
    - Lower battery impact
    - Familiar for maintainers
  end note
endif

if (Go framework?) then
  :net/http vs Fiber;
  note right
    Fiber provides Express-like APIs,
    built-in routing and middleware,
    and fast onboarding.
  end note
  :Fiber selected;
endif

if (Database?) then
  :SQLite vs PostgreSQL vs files;
  note right
    - Embedded, zero config database
    - Native FTS5 full-text search
    - WAL for non-blocking reads
    - Single file backup model
    - Great for single-user workloads
  end note
  :SQLite (WAL + FTS5) selected;
endif

if (Frontend framework?) then
  :React vs Vue vs Svelte vs Vanilla;
  note right
    | Framework | Weight | Separation | Build |
    | React | 45 KB | JSX | yes |
    | Vue 3 | 30 KB | SFC | yes |
    | Svelte | 5 KB | SFC | yes |
    | Vanilla | 0 KB | full | no |
  end note
  :Vanilla JS modules selected;
  note right
    - No build pipeline required
    - Clear module separation
    - Minimal runtime footprint
    - TipTap works standalone
  end note
endif

if (Rich editor?) then
  :TipTap vs Quill vs ProseMirror;
  note right
    - TipTap is ProseMirror-based
    - Native image paste support
    - Extensible command model
    - Free open source
    - Works with CDN ESM setup
  end note
  :TipTap selected;
endif

:Final stack validated;
note right
  Go + Fiber + SQLite + Vanilla JS + TipTap
  on Termux (Android)
end note

stop
@enduml